<code>assert element != null => element.equals(this.peek());</code>

However, the comment suggests that the added element should be equal to the last element in the queue, but `peek()` returns the first element in the queue. To correctly reflect the comment, we need to check the last element. Since the queue is circular, the last element can be accessed using the `end` index. Here is the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert element != null => element.equals(this.query((end - 1 + maxElements) % maxElements));</code>

This assert statement checks if the added element is equal to the last element in the queue, considering the circular nature of the queue.
